messages:
alex: Noticed flaky behaviour in the browser SDK when auth refresh happens during an SSE stream. Sometimes final token chunks never arrive and UI shows partial messages.

elaine: Saw a repro in our onboarding sample app. If the token refresh fires while the server is mid-event, the client parser doesn't get the trailing bytes.

alex: Repro steps I used: 1) open long-running streaming call, 2) stub token expiry to trigger refresh at ~15s, 3) server writes a multi-line event in two writes (first write ends mid-line), 4) client aborts and reconnects. Outcome: first event truncated and no [DONE].

jon: Do you use fetch + ReadableStream getReader() and a textDecoder split on "\n\n"? That pattern is brittle if underlying read returns partial UTF-8 codepoints.

alex: Yep. Parser code (simplified): ```js
const r = await fetch(url, { signal });
const reader = r.body.getReader();
const dec = new TextDecoder();
let buf = '';
while(true){
  const {done, value} = await reader.read();
  if(done) break;
  buf += dec.decode(value, {stream: true});
  const events = buf.split('\n\n');
  buf = events.pop() || '';
  events.forEach(parseEvent);
}
```

kevin: Two failure modes: (A) abort() leaves an unread partial chunk in the network stack (browser-specific), (B) decoder.stream=true yields trailing high-byte sequences that only complete on next chunk. If we flush on abort we might still produce broken utf8.

ben: Possible fixes: 1) on abort/close, call dec.decode(undefined) to flush remaining bytes properly before handling the leftover buffer, 2) on abort emit a special partial event so apps can decide to re-request/resume.

elaine: Flushing via dec.decode() is sensible. Also we should avoid unilaterally aborting streams from the SDK auth routine. The SDK today calls controller.abort() during refresh, which is what triggers the issue.

alex: I'm inclined to implement both: decoder flush + sdk-managed graceful refresh API. For immediate patch I'll add decoder.flush on done/abort and emit a `__partial_event` with raw text.

jon: We need parity: python SDK uses urllib3 streaming iter_lines which has its own chunking semantics. Add equivalent tests in python repo that simulate mid-event disconnect.

kevin: Add test harness that spins up a tiny test server that writes: `data: hello\n\n` then `data: par` then delay then `tial\n\n[data: [DONE]]`. Then simulate client-side abort after the `par` write. Assert parser emits `hello` then emits `par` as partial-on-abort.

ben: Also add a small recommended pattern to sample-app README: prefer letting short-lived streams finish; if you do need to force-refresh, call `sdk.requestGracefulReconnect()` which will try a parallel token refresh and signal the app with `onPartial` callback.

maria: We should document the semantics in the SDK CHANGELOG and onboarding docs: what `onPartial` means, how to resume safely, and why Last-Event-ID would be better long-term.

alex: I'll open a Node SDK PR that: 1) flushes decoder on stream close/abort, 2) emits `__SSE_PARTIAL__` event with raw trailing text, 3) adds tests under tests/streaming/abort-partial.test.js. Draft PR link when ready.

devex-bot: New issue created: SDK-2462 (Browser SDK graceful refresh and partial-flush behavior).

elaine: For browser UX, add a UI hint in sample-app: when partial emitted, show a subtle "message still streaming" banner and auto-attempt resume. Helps reduce confusion for new devs.

jon: I'll write a short ADR for standard streaming semantics across SDKs: "streams must not be aborted by default during auth refresh; SDKs should provide a managed reconnect hook and a partial-event signal for apps to handle resumptions."

kevin: If we go the route of adding stream IDs/offsets server-side, SDKs can send the last-offset on reconnect so the server can patch missing tokens. File an infra RFC for that separately.

alex: Created PR draft: github.com/redwood-inference/node-sdk/pull/802 with tests. Will add Python + Browser follow-ups.

maria: Nice. Also add a tiny entry to the onboarding checklist: "Avoid abort-on-refresh; use retry/resume pattern." New hires hit this in the first week.

alex: Will update the sample-app README and link the ADR + PRs. Will also attach a short screencapture of the failing flow for triage.
